  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given three **distinct** integers A,B,A, B,A,B, and CCC.\n\nFind **any** integer X&nbsp;(0≤X&lt;230)X \\ (0 \\leq X &lt; 2^{30})X&nbsp;(0≤X&lt;230) such that:\n\n(A⊕X)&lt;(B⊕X)&lt;(C⊕X)(A \\oplus X) \\lt (B \\oplus X) \\lt (C \\oplus X)(A⊕X)&lt;(B⊕X)&lt;(C⊕X), where ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the Bitwise XOR operation.\n\nIf no such XXX exists, print −1-1−1 instead.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT, the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains three space-separated integers A,B,A, B,A,B, and CCC.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a single integer on a new line, the value of XXX that satisfies the above conditions or −1-1−1 if no such XXX exists.\n\n\nIf multiple such XXX satisfy the condition, you may print any.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤A,B,C&lt;2301 \\leq A, B, C \\lt 2^{30}1≤A,B,C&lt;230",
      "A,B,CA, B, CA,B,C are **distinct**."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n1 2 3\n3 1 2\n3 2 1",
        "output": "4\n-1\n3",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: For X=4X = 4X=4,\n\nA⊕X=1⊕4 =5A \\oplus X = 1 \\oplus 4 \\ = 5A⊕X=1⊕4 =5\nB⊕X=2⊕4 =6B \\oplus X = 2 \\oplus 4 \\ = 6B⊕X=2⊕4 =6\nC⊕X=3⊕4 =7C \\oplus X = 3 \\oplus 4 \\ = 7C⊕X=3⊕4 =7\n\nThus, (A⊕X)<(B⊕X)<(C⊕X)(A \\oplus X) \\lt (B \\oplus X) \\lt (C \\oplus X)(A⊕X)<(B⊕X)<(C⊕X).\nTest case 222: No X (0≤X<230)X \\ (0 \\leq X \\lt 2^{30})X (0≤X<230) exists that satisfies the above conditions.\nTest case 333: For X=3X = 3X=3,\n\nA⊕X=3⊕3 =0A \\oplus X = 3 \\oplus 3 \\ = 0A⊕X=3⊕3 =0\nB⊕X=2⊕3 =1B \\oplus X = 2 \\oplus 3 \\ = 1B⊕X=2⊕3 =1\nC⊕X=1⊕3 =2C \\oplus X = 1 \\oplus 3 \\ = 2C⊕X=1⊕3 =2\n\nThus, (A⊕X)<(B⊕X)<(C⊕X)(A \\oplus X) \\lt (B \\oplus X) \\lt (C \\oplus X)(A⊕X)<(B⊕X)<(C⊕X)."
      }
    ]
  },
